{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The fix is applied and submitted. The submission endpoint returned a 200 response. I haven't sent test requests through the frontend or checked how traffic behaves afterward.\n\n**Cause:** The `frontend` service selects pods by the label `service-route=frontend`, and the `search` pods also had that label. About half of the frontend traffic was therefore going to search pods, which don't serve the frontend port (5000), so those requests failed.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I removed the stray `service-route` label from the `search` deployment's pod template.\n- I set the `frontend` service selector back to `io.kompose.service: frontend`.\n\nAfterwards the `frontend` endpoints list only the frontend pod, and `search` runs as a separate pod."}}
